 "final_text": "`/work/fateh_024.lean` now compiles with no errors and no `sorry` warning. I replaced the single `sorry` and changed nothing else.\n\nThe proof uses the fact that \u211a/\u2124 is divisible, so every element is an `H.index`-fold multiple of another element:\n\n1. Let `n = H.index`. It is nonzero because `H` has finite index.\n2. For any `x = [q]` in \u211a/\u2124, take `y = [q / n]`. Mathlib's `AddSubgroup.nsmul_index_mem` gives `n \u2022 y \u2208 H`, since `H` is normal (the group is commutative).\n3. `n \u2022 y = [n \u00b7 (q / n)] = [q] = x`, so `x \u2208 H`. Hence `H = \u22a4`.\n\nI didn't use `axiom`, `native_decide`, `#eval` or metaprogramming.",
